# On Your Left — environment variable template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.gitignore` ignores
# `.env` and `.env.*` and un-ignores this file, so the template is committed and
# the values never are. Never put a real secret here: this repository is public,
# secret scanning with push protection is on, and a pushed commit is permanent
# regardless of what a later commit deletes.
#
# `bash scripts/check-env-example.sh` (rule ENV001) fails if any source file
# under `apps/` or `packages/` reads a variable that is not listed here, so this
# file cannot silently fall behind the code.
#
# Format: one `NAME=placeholder` per line. A variable with no meaningful
# placeholder still gets an entry with an empty value, because the entry is what
# documents that the variable exists.
#
# --- Phase 1 -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Phase 1 is entirely local: no server, no account and no API key (owner
# decision D6). The one entry below is not an exception to that — it is the
# address of a *static file* on storage this project controls, and there is no
# key, no account and no metering behind it.

# The PMTiles basemap archive the ride map reads (#63).
#
# ADR 0010 decision D-1: the Protomaps basemap as a PMTiles archive on
# Cloudflare R2, behind Cloudflare's CDN. An `https:` URL to the archive itself;
# no `pmtiles://` prefix, which the client adds. Anything else — unset, empty,
# unparseable or `http:` — means "no basemap", and the ride detail view says so
# in words rather than drawing an empty grid.
#
# ⚠️ **Nothing is published to point this at yet.** #53 owns copying a pinned
# daily build into our own bucket and verifying it against the published BLAKE3
# digest. Until it lands this stays empty, which is the honest state rather than
# a hole: `apps/web/src/map/basemap.ts` treats it as "no map configured".
#
# ⚠️ **Do not point it at somebody else's host.** Protomaps' own downloads page
# says hotlinking "are discouraged" and "URLs may change", and ADR 0010 D-1 is
# explicit: copy the archive, do not hotlink it. The origin of whatever is here
# is the *only* host the map is permitted to reach, which
# `apps/web/src/map/basemap.test.ts` asserts.
VITE_BASEMAP_PMTILES_URL=

# --- The browser gate, not the product --------------------------------------
#
# A hosted PMTiles archive for the browser gate to measure against (#63).
#
# ⚠️ **Not read by anything that ships.** It is read by
# `apps/web/browser/map.browser.spec.ts`, which is Playwright rather than Vite —
# hence no `VITE_` prefix, which would only put it in a bundle. Unset, it skips
# the hosted block of `pnpm run test:browser`, and CI leaves it unset: a gate
# that needs somebody else's CDN is a gate that fails on an aeroplane. Set to an
# `https:` archive URL, that block renders the real basemap in the pinned
# Chromium and takes #63's eighth measurement, time to first painted tile.
#
# ⚠️ Set but malformed is an **error**, not a skip. "Nothing configured" and
# "configured wrongly" are different states and only the first is a reason to
# measure nothing — `apps/web/browser/hosted-archive.ts` says why.
#
# ⚠️ Deliberately a different name from VITE_BASEMAP_PMTILES_URL above. Reusing
# that one would silently put a network dependency into the browser gate for
# everybody who has a basemap configured for their own development build.
OYL_HOSTED_BASEMAP_URL=

# --- The device probe, not the product ---------------------------------------
#
# The local TCP port `adb forward` is holding open onto the shell's WebView
# DevTools socket (#410).
#
# ⚠️ **Not read by anything that ships, and not read by any gate either.** It is
# read by `apps/mobile/tools/webview-probe.mjs`, which needs `adb`, a phone with
# developer options on and a **debug** build — so it can never run in CI and is
# not part of `check:repo`. `docs/validation/0002-android-shell-and-game.md`
# Part P is the procedure it serves.
#
# Unset, the probe uses 9222, which is what `adb forward tcp:9222 …` gives you
# and what every DevTools example on the internet assumes. Set it when 9222 is
# already taken on your machine, and forward to the same number.
OYL_DEVTOOLS_PORT=9222

# --- The realism spike's asset pipeline, not the product (#457) --------------
#
# The Blender executable `apps/web/tools/realism/process-assets.ts` runs
# headless (`-b --python`). ⚠️ SPIKE BRANCH ONLY, never merged: Blender is a
# tool and never a dependency, and no gate runs it. Unset, the script uses the
# macOS application path.
BLENDER=
